  <data name="UIModel_DiagTrackService_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Enable the telemetry service</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_DiagTrackService_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Configure "Connected User Experiences and Telemetry" (DiagTrack) service and connection for the Unified Telemetry Client Outbound Traffic. Disabling "Connected User Experiences and Telemetry" service (DiagTrack) can cause you not being able to get Xbox achievements anymore and affects Feedback Hub.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_DiagnosticDataLevel_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Configure Windows level of diagnostic data gathering</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_DiagnosticDataLevel_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>As a part of using Windows, your device sends Microsoft a limited set of data that is necessary to keep your device and operating system secure, up to date, and working as expected.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_DiagnosticDataLevel_Title_1" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Default</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_DiagnosticDataLevel_Title_2" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Minimal</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_ErrorReporting_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Configure Windows Error Reporting</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_ErrorReporting_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Error reporting feature enables users to notify Microsoft of application faults, kernel faults, unresponsive applications, and other application specific problems. Microsoft can use error reporting feature to provide customers with troubleshooting information, solutions, or updates for their specific problems.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_FeedbackFrequency_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Configure feedback frequency</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_FeedbackFrequency_Title_1" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Automatically</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_FeedbackFrequency_Title_2" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Never</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_FeedbackFrequency_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Choose how often Windows asks for your feedback.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_ScheduledTasks_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Enable diagnostic tracking tasks</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_ScheduledTasks_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Enable following telemetry related scheduled tasks in Task Scheduler: MareBackup, Microsoft Compatibility Appraiser, StartupAppTask, ProgramDataUpdater, Proxy, Consolidator, UsbCeip, Microsoft-Windows-DiskDiagnosticDataCollector, Microsoft-Windows-DiskDiagnosticDataCollector, MapsToastTask, MapsUpdateTask, FamilySafetyMonitor, FamilySafetyRefreshTask, XblGameSaveTask.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_SigninInfo_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Use sign-in info to automatically finish setting up device after an update</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_SigninInfo_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Some updates require you to restart your PC and afterwards sign in to Windows in order to finish installing update, which means you might not be able to use your PC until update is finished. Windows helps prevents this by allowing Windows to use your sign in info to create a special token. This token is used to automatically sign in after a restart, finish setting up your PC, and then lock your PC to keep your account and personal info safe.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_LanguageListAccess_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Let websites show me locally relevant content by accessing language my list</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_AdvertisingID_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Let apps show me personalized ads by using my advertising ID</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_WindowsWelcomeExperience_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Show Windows welcome experiences after updates and occasionally when signed in to show what's new suggested</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_WindowsTips_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Get tips and suggestions when using Windows</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_SettingsSuggestedContent_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Show suggested content in the Settings app</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_AppsSilentInstalling_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Enable automatic installing suggested apps</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_AppsSilentInstalling_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Windows may silently download and install some suggested apps from the Microsoft Store without any user confirmation.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_WhatsNewInWindows_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Show ways to get the most out of Windows and finish setting up this device</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_WhatsNewInWindows_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Windows may display a "Let's finish setting up your device" prompt occasionally that displays additional services that user may set up.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_TailoredExperiences_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Enable tailored experiences</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_TailoredExperiences_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Let Microsoft offer you tailored expereinces based on diagnostic data setting you have chosen.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_BingSearch_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Enable Bing search in the Start Menu</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_StartRecommendationsTips_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Show recommendations for tips, shortcuts, new apps, and more in the Start menu</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_StartAccountNotifications_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Show Microsoft account-related notifications on Start Menu in the Start menu</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UwpPage_AboutAppIcon.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Choose UWP app to uninstall. UWP apps list is rendered in real-time with their native icon logos taken from Windows. That means that the UWP apps list is not pre-prepared like in other similar apps.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_HEVC_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Install HEVC Video codec (H.265)</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_HEVC_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>HEVC Video codec will be downloaded for an official Microsoft server. This codec allows you to open images and videos in .heif and .hevc formats, respectively.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_XboxGameBar_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Enable Xbox Game Bar</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_XboxGameBar_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Disable Xbox Game Bar app (even if you uninstalled it before) to prevent a popup message "You'll need a new app to open this ms-gamingoverlay".</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_XboxGameTips_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Xbox Game Bar tips</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_GPUScheduling_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Enable Hardware-accelerated GPU scheduling</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_GPUScheduling_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Reduce latency and improve performance. You'll need to restart your PC to have your changes take effect. With Hardware-Accelerated GPU Scheduling feature, GPU's scheduling processor and memory (VRAM) take over the same work and runs it in batches to render the frames. This allows your GPU to reduce load on your CPU and improve latency, potentially making your PC run better. However, don’t expect GPU hardware scheduling to have a significant impact on your computer performance.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_CleanupTask_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Create Windows Cleanup scheduled task</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_CleanupTask_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>This function creates "Windows Cleanup" (main task) and "Windows Cleanup Notification" (task to generate a pop-up notification) tasks in the Task Scheduler to clean up unused files and Windows updates. A native notification prompting you to run the task will pop up before cleanup begins. The task runs every 30 days. Windows Script Host must be enabled for the task to run. A native Windows notification will appear when complete.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_SoftwareDistributionTask_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Create SoftwareDistribution scheduled task</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_SoftwareDistributionTask_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>This function creates "SoftwareDistribution" task in the Task Scheduler to clean up %SystemRoot%\SoftwareDistribution\Download folder where Windows updates installation files are downloaded. The task will wait until Windows Update service has finished running. The task runs every 90 days. Windows Script Host must be enabled for the task to run. A native Windows notification will appear when complete.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_TempTask_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Create Temp scheduled task</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_TempTask_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>This function creates "Temp" task in the Task Scheduler to clean up %TEMP% folder. Only files older than one day will be deleted. The task runs every 60 days. Windows Script Host must be enabled for the task to run. A native Windows notification will appear when complete.</value>
  </data>
